# Future work tracking

When work is **deferred**, **out of scope for the current task**, or **discovered during implementation**, record it so it is not lost. Pick the right doc — do not default to chat-only notes.

**Canonical sources:**

- [docs/FRD.md](../../docs/FRD.md) — product roadmap (**Today** / **Planned**)
- [docs/TECH-DEBT.md](../../docs/TECH-DEBT.md) — bugs, quality gaps, fix-up and investigation items **an agent can close**
- [docs/HUMAN-TASKS.md](../../docs/HUMAN-TASKS.md) — work whose verification **requires a person**, physical hardware, or a real-world measurement

## Decide where it goes

Ask the questions in this order. The first "yes" wins.

**1. Can this only be verified by a human?** → **HUMAN-TASKS**

Printing a physical label and measuring it; judging whether output looks right against a real-world reference; anything needing a device, account, or environment an agent cannot reach. Priority is independent of the doc — a High item can live here.

**2. Does it change what the product offers?** → **FRD** (Planned)

| Track in **FRD** (Planned) | Track in **TECH-DEBT** (Open) |
|---|---|
| New capability users would choose or notice | Known bug or regression |
| Intentional product direction | Existing behavior that should work but does not meet quality bar |
| New vial size, mode, template, account layer, etc. | Export/render quality gap reproducible in code or a browser |
| “We will build X later” as a feature | Refactor, cleanup, or investigation follow-up |
| Changes **what** the product offers | Fixes **how well** shipped behavior works |

**Examples:**

- Landing page, calculator-only mode, 10 ml vial → **FRD** Planned
- Export margin too large on a physical B21 print; text less crisp than native Niimbot text → **HUMAN-TASKS** (needs a print and a measurement)
- Reducer accepts an unrepresentable unit pairing; two sources of truth in the print catalog → **TECH-DEBT**
- Shipped print setup but missing first-run wizard polish → usually **TECH-DEBT** unless it is a committed product milestone

## When unclear

If the item could reasonably belong to two of the three, **ask the developer** which doc to use before adding it. Briefly state the options and your lean.

Do not duplicate the same item across docs unless the user explicitly wants both angles (rare — avoid by default).

## When adding an entry

- **FRD:** value-led **why + what**; match existing Planned tone (see `functional-requirements.mdc`).
- **TECH-DEBT:** symptom, priority, status, and concrete hypotheses or files to inspect.
- **HUMAN-TASKS:** what is blocked on, plus a **step-by-step procedure** the human can follow without re-deriving the problem — and, where a blind change would be harmful, say so explicitly.
- On the same change set when you **ship** the fix: move TECH-DEBT items to **Resolved**; move FRD items from **Planned** to **Today**.

## What an agent may and may not do with HUMAN-TASKS

An agent **may** prepare an item: write or sharpen the procedure, narrow the hypotheses, add the code path a measurement would exercise.

An agent **may not** mark an item done, or apply a speculative fix in place of the measurement. A blind fix to a hardware item is worse than none — it consumes the physical test that would have told you something.
